24 \u964 \'f4\u949 \'e5\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u954 \'ea\u945 \'e1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8054 ? \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u955 \'eb\u959 \'ef\u953 \'e9\u960 \'f0\u959 \'ef\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8059 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u962 \'f2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   [Ms. \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u960 \'f0\u959 \'ef\u955 \'eb\u953 \'e9\u964 \'f4\u953 \'e9\u954 \'ea\u959 \'ef\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8150 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u962 \'f2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u964 \'f4\u949 \'e5\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u954 \'ea\u945 \'e1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8054 ? \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u955 \'eb\u959 \'ef\u953 \'e9\u960 \'f0\u959 \'ef\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8150 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u962 \'f2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  !]); \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  inc.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   (erste Sentenz) {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666v/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 \u7977 ? \u8000 ?\u961 ?\u952 ?\u8057 ?\u948 d\u959 ?\u958 ?\u959 ?\u962 ? \u960 p\u8055 ?\u963 s\u964 t\u953 ?\u962 ? \u964 t\u8182 ?\u957 ? \u7936 ?\u955 ?\u951 ?\u952 ?\u8182 ?\u962 ? \u935 ?\u961 ?\u953 ?\u963 s\u964 t\u953 ?\u945 a\u957 ?\u8182 ?\u957 ? \u948 d\u8055 ?\u967 ?\u945 a \u7956 ?\u961 ?\u947 ?\u969 ?\u957 ? \u7936 ?\u947 ?\u945 a\u952 ?\u8182 ?\u957 ? \u957 ?\u949 e\u954 ?\u961 ?\u8049 ? \u7952 ?\u963 s\u964 t\u953 ?\u957 ?, \u8033 ?\u956 \'b5\u959 ?\u8055 ?\u969 ?\u962 ? \u954 ?\u945 a\u8054 ? \u964 t\u8048 ? \u7956 ?\u961 ?\u947 ?\u945 a \u967 ?\u969 ?\u961 ?\u8054 ?\u962 ? \u960 p\u8055 ?\u963 s\u964 t\u949 e\u969 ?\u962 ? \u957 ?\u949 e\u954 ?\u961 ?\u8049 ? \u949 e\u7984 ?\u963 s\u953 ?\u957 ? \u954 ?\u964 t\u955 ?.}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  des.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   (letzte Sentenz) {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666v/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 \u924 ?\u8052 ? \u956 \'b5\u949 e\u947 ?\u945 a\u955 ?\u959 ?\u966 f\u961 ?\u959 ?\u957 ?\u8135 ?\u962 ? (Ms. \u956 \'b5\u949 e\u947 ?\u945 a\u955 ?\u959 ?\u966 f\u961 ?\u8057 ?\u957 ?\u8131 ?) \u956 \'b5\u951 ?\u948 d\u8050 ? \u960 p\u8118 ?\u957 ? \u966 f\u945 a\u957 ?\u964 t\u8049 ?\u950 ?\u959 ?\u965 ? \u8230 \'85 \u7952 ?\u954 ?\u960 p\u8051 ?\u963 s\u949 e\u953 ? \u954 ?\u945 a\u8054 ? \u964 t\u8182 ?\u957 ? \u956 \'b5\u949 e\u964 t\u961 ?\u8055 ?\u969 ?\u957 ?.}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   Es handelt sich um 33 biblische und patristische Sentenzen, meist asketischen Inhalts. Zum Incipit vgl. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Ioannes Damascenus}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Expositio fidei, cap. 82, 60\endash 61, ed. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Kotter\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Schriften II, S. 184, 60\endash 61; CPG III 8043. Z\u228 \'e4hlung der Sentenzen am Rand: \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u945 \'e1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u180 \'b4\endash \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u955 \'eb\u946 \'e2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u180 \'b4 (!). \endash  Dasselbe Incipit (hier ohne Prolog) auch in einem Florilegium mit 281 Kapiteln (Florilegium \u8222 \'84Damascenianum\ldblquote ), das u. a. in Cod. Vatop. 13, ff. 129r\endash 147v (vgl. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 E. Lamberz\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Katalog der griechischen Handschriften des Athos\-klo\-sters Vatopedi, Band 1: Codices 1\endash 102 [\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u922 \'ca\u945 \'e1\u964 \'f4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8049 ?\-\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u955 \'eb\u959 \'ef\u947 \'e3\u959 \'ef\u953 \'e9\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u949 \'e5\u955 \'eb\u955 \'eb\u951 \'e7\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \-\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u957 \'ed\u953 \'e9\u954 \'ea\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8061 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u957 \'ed\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u967 \'f7\u949 \'e5\u953 \'e9\u961 \'f1\u959 \'ef\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \-\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u947 \'e3\u961 \'f1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8049 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u966 \'f6\u969 \'f9\u957 \'ed\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u913 \'c1\u947 \'e3\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8055 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u959 \'ef\u965 \'f5\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \u8185 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u961 \'f1\u959 \'ef\u965 \'f5\u962 \'f2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   2], Thessaloniki 2006, S. 87\endash 94, hier S. 90), vorhanden ist, vgl. dazu \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 P. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 G\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 \u233 \'e9\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 hin\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Collections de \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  kephalaia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   mona\-stiques: naissance et succ\u232 \'e8s d\rquote un genre entre cr\u233 \'e9ation originale, plagiat et floril\u232 \'e8ge, in: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 A. Rigo / P. Ermilov / M. Trizio \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Hrsg.), Theologica minora. The Minor Genres of Byzan\-tine Theological Literature (\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u914 \'c2\u933 \'d5\u918 \'c6\u913 \'c1\u925 \'cd\u932 \'d4\u921 \'c9\u927 \'cf\u931 \'d3\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Studies in Byzantine History and Civilization 8), \u8249 \'8bTurnhout 2013\u8250 \'9b, S. 1\endash 50, hier S. 39 mit Anm. 180 und S. 47.}

