 \'e5\u953 \'e9\u964 \'f4\u945 \'e1\u953 \'e9\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \u7952 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u957 \'ed\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \u7948 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u961 \'f1\u947 \'e3\u949 \'e5\u953 \'e9\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u954 \'ea\u964 \'f4\u955 \'eb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ., ed. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Schwartz, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  a. O., S. 93, 5\endash 8. \endash  (f. 89v) Randscholion (zu v. 998); \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  inc. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666v/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 \u932 ?\u8056 ?\u957 ? \u7936 ?\u961 ?\u957 ?\u8056 ?\u957 ? \u964 t\u959 ?\u8166 ?\u964 t\u959 ?\u957 ? \u8017 ?\u960 p\u8051 ?\u946 \'df\u945 a\u955 ?\u949 e \u8001 ? \u7961 ?\u961 ?\u956 \'b5\u8134 ?\u962 ? \u8000 ?\u961 ?\u947 ?\u953 ?\u950 ?\u8057 ?\u956 \'b5\u949 e\u957 ?\u959 ?\u962 ? \u7944 ?\u964 t\u961 ?\u949 e\u8150 ?, \u7952 ?\u960 p\u949 e\u8054 ? \u960 p\u961 ?\u8057 ?\u947 ?\u959 ?\u957 ?\u959 ?\u962 ? \u945 a\u8016 ?\u964 t\u959 ?\u8166 ? \u8001 ? \u928 ?\u8051 ?\u955 ?\u959 ?\u968 ? \u7974 ?\u957 ? \u954 ?\u964 t\u955 ?.}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  des.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u948 \'e4\u953 \'e9\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8048 ? \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u964 \'f4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8134 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u962 \'f2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u947 \'e3\u965 \'f5\u957 \'ed\u945 \'e1\u953 \'e9\u954 \'ea\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8056 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u962 \'f2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u945 \'e1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8016 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u964 \'f4\u959 \'ef\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8166 ? \u7944 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u949 \'e5\u961 \'f1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8057 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u960 \'f0\u951 \'e7\u962 \'f2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u956 \'ec\u959 \'ef\u953 \'e9\u967 \'f7\u949 \'e5\u965 \'f5\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \-\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u952 \'e8\u949 \'e5\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8055 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u963 \'f3\u945 \'e1\u962 \'f2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u960 \'f0\u945 \'e1\u961 \'f1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \rquote  \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u945 \'e1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8016 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u964 \'f4\u959 \'ef\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8166 ?. Zum Incipit vgl. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Dindorf\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , a. O., II, S. 251, 15\endash 18, und \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Schwartz\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , a. O., S. 198, 11\endash 13. \endash  Am Textende in blassroter Tinte: \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u932 \'d4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8051 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u955 \'eb\u959 \'ef\u962 \'f2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u964 \'f4\u959 \'ef\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8166 ? \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u960 \'f0\u945 \'e1\u961 \'f1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8057 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u957 \'ed\u964 \'f4\u959 \'ef\u962 \'f2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u946 \'e2\u953 \'e9\u946 \'e2\u955 \'eb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8055 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u959 \'ef\u965 \'f5\u903 ?\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \u8008 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u961 \'f1\u949 \'e5\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \-\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u963 \'f3\u964 \'f4\u949 \'e5\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8055 ?\-\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u959 \'ef\u965 \'f5\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u948 \'e4\u961 \'f1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8049 ?\-\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u956 \'ec\u945 \'e1\u964 \'f4\u959 \'ef\u962 \'f2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , \u7976 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u955 \'eb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8051 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u954 \'ea\u964 \'f4\u961 \'f1\u945 \'e1\u962 \'f2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   (!) \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u964 \'f4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8051 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u955 \'eb\u959 \'ef\u962 \'f2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . Unmittelbar darunter zwei Invokationen in Zw\u246 \'f6lfsilbern vom Kopisten (s. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  S\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  /II. Teil), ebenfalls in blass\-roter Tinte. \endash  (ff. 112v\endash 113v) leer, ausgenommen Eintrag auf f. 113v (s. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  S\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  /II. Teil, d). 
