\pard\sl360\slmult1\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  2. (ff. 2v\endash 11r) De modo recte scribendi (Ms. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  De modo recte scribendi tractatus feliciter incipit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ); inc.\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24   {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 \u8249 \'8bO\u8250 \'9brthographia ut Quintiliano placet est recte scribendi scientia. Hec vero duplex est: altera enim ut nitide, altera ut recte scribas}}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17  eqs.}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   des. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  et si omnes consenserite, ego non negabo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , vgl. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Kremsm\u252 \'fcnster, Benediktinerstift, Cod. CC 134 (vgl.\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  P. O. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Kristeller\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Iter Italicum. Accedunt Alia Itinera. A Finding List of Uncatalogued or Incompletely Catalogued Humanistic Manuscripts of the Renaissance in Italian and Other Libraries, III [Alia Itinera I]. Australia to Germany, London / Leiden 1983, S. 23); \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 vgl.\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  BSB, Clm 24563, ff. 1r\u8722 -6r, dort weitergef\u252 \'fchrt bis f. 6v (vgl. G. L. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Bursill-Hall\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , A Census of Medieval Latin Grammatical Manuscripts [Grammatica Speculativa 4], Stuttgart / Bad Cannstatt 1981, S. 161 [Nr. 237]). \endash  (ff. 11v\endash 12r) leer. \endash  Anschlie\u223 \'dfend: (f. 12v) griech. Sentenzen mit lat. Interlinear\u252 \'fcbersetzung; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  inc.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666v/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 \u922 ?\u945 a\u955 ?\u8182 ?\u962 ? \u960 p\u959 ?\u953 ?\u949 e\u8150 ?\u957 ? \u7952 ?\u963 s\u964 t\u953 ? \u954 ?\u945 a\u955 ?\u8057 ?\u957 ?\u903 ? \u954 ?\u945 a\u954 ?\u8182 ?\u962 ? \u948 d\u8050 ? \u960 p\u959 ?\u953 ?\u949 e\u8150 ?\u957 ? \u954 ?\u945 a\u954 ?\u8055 ?\u962 ? (!) \u7952 ?\u963 s\u964 t\u953 ? \u954 ?\u964 t\u955 ?.}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  des.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u924 \'cc\u951 \'e7\u948 \'e4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8050 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u957 \'ed\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \u7940 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u947 \'e3\u945 \'e1\u957 \'ed\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Bene facere est bonum, male autem facere malum est\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   eqs. des. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  ne quid nimis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  (f. 13r\endash v) griech. Alphabet und Diphthonge, Pater noster (griech.); \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  des. imperfecte\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u964 \'f4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8056 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u957 \'ed\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \u7940 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u961 \'f1\u964 \'f4\u959 \'ef\u957 \'ed\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \u7969 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u956 \'ec\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8182 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u957 \'ed\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u964 \'f4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8056 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u957 \'ed\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \u7952 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u960 \'f0\u953 \'e9\u959 \'ef\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8059 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u963 \'f3\u953 \'e9\u959 \'ef\u957 \'ed\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u948 \'e4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8056 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u962 \'f2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \u7969 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u956 \'ec\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8150 ?\plain \f2\lang1032\fs24 \u957 \'ed\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Klassifikation der griech. Konsonanten.}

