\pard\sl360\slmult1\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  1. (ff. 225r\endash 225v, 10. Z.; ff. 226v, 25. Z.\endash 232v) \u8249 \'8b{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Mallius Theodorus}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , De metris\u8250 \'9b (Ms. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  De sufficiencia artis metrice aliqua sunt notanda\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ), ed. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 H. Keil\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Scriptores Artis metricae. Marius Victorinus, Maximus Victorinus, Caesius Bassus \u8230 \'85 Mallius Theodorus, Fragmenta et excerpta metrica (Grammatici Latini VI), Leipzig 1874, S. 585\endash 601; ed. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 F. Romanini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Malli Theodori De metris (Bibliotheca Weidmanniana VI, Collectanea Grammatica Latina [CGL] 4), Hildesheim / Z\u252 \'fcrich / New York 2007. (f. 225r, 24. Z.) Textauslassung: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Romanini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , S. 7, 8 (I 3) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  appellari oportere\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   (Ms. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  debere\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ). [\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Scribimus igitur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \u8230 \'85 S. 11, 4 (II 6) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  pronuntiandi forma expetit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Posicione longe syllabe\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .
\par \pard\sl360\slmult1\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 (f. 225r, 1.\endash 24. Z.) cap. I; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  des\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . I 3, s. oben. \endash  (f. 225r, 24. Z.\endash 225v, 10. Z.) cap. II (Ms. ohne Titel; Anfangsworte in Majuskel als \u220 \'dcberschrift); \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  inc\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . II 6, s. oben. 
\par \pard\sl360\slmult1\fi0\li0\tx420\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \tab (ff. 225v, 10. Z.\endash 226v, 24. Z.) zwischen \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Romanini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , S. 13, 15 (II 7) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  vasto Ciclopis in antro \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Verg., Aen. III 647) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  item vasto\u8249 \'8bs\u8250 \'9bque ab rupe Ciclopas\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   (Verg., Aen. III 617) und S. 13, 17 (III 1) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Penthasillabos etiam quidam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   folgende in den Ausgaben nicht vorhandenen Abschnitte: (f. 225v, 10.\endash 25. Z.) prosodisches Exzerpt (Ms. ohne Titel; Text direkt an das Vorangehende anschlie\u223 \'dfend); inc.\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24   {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Aliquando proicienda ex metro: ponite spes sibi quisque (Verg., Aen. XI 309), ne sit amphimacrus pro dactilo}}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17  eqs.}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   des. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  sicut etiam \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  etiam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   am Rand) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  constravit littora Xerxes.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \endash  (f. 225v, 26.\endash 27. Z.) Definition von Arsis und Thesis (Ms. ohne Titel; Text direkt an das Vorangehende anschlie\u223 \'dfend): {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Arsis elevatio, thesis depositio dicitur, ut Roma: RO arsis, MA thesis.}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \endash  (ff. 225v, 27. Z.\endash 226v, 12. Z.) \u8249 \'8bDe pedibus\u8250 \'9b (Ms. ohne Titel; Text direkt an das Vorangehende anschlie\u223 \'dfend); inc. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[3].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Nullus pes apud Lattinos ultra quatuor sillabas habet}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24   \u8230 \'85 ex his nomina habent viginti octo quos grammatici tractant. Bissillabi sunt quatuor: spondeus \plain \f4\lang1037\fs24 \u1472 \'d0\u1472 \'d0\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 , pirricheus \u183 \'b7\u183 \'b7, trocheus \plain \f4\lang1037\fs24 \u1472 \'d0\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  \u183 \'b7, iambus \u183 \'b7\plain \f4\lang1037\fs24 \u1472 \'d0\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  tertius epitritus \plain \f4\lang1037\fs24 \u1472 \'d0\u1472 \'d0\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  \u183 \'b7\plain \f4\lang1037\fs24 \u1472 \'d0\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24 , quartus epitritus \plain \f4\lang1037\fs24 \u1472 \'d0\u1472 \'d0\u1472 \'d0\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  \u183 \'b7\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  De quinque sillabis sunt triginta duo synzygiae \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Ms. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  zinzigi\plain \f7\i\lang1024\fs24 \u281 \'ea\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ), \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  de sex sillabis LXIII \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  eqs. des. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  triplus I, sextupli VII, epitriti IIII.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \endash  (f. 226v, 13.\endash 24. Z.) \u8249 \'8bDe caesuris\u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Ms. ohne Titel; Text direkt an das Vorangehende anschlie\u223 \'dfend); inc. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[2].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Cesure versuum sunt quatuor a(u)t(em) (!): districtus, qui in scansione pedum dictionem nunquam integram deditur}}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[2].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17  eqs.}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   des. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  aut Ararim Parthus bibet aut Germania Tigrim \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Verg., Buc. I 62). Abschnitt mit demselben Incipit auch in Cod. Par. lat. 7559, ff. 67r\endash 69r, vgl. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 M. Passalacqua\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , I codici di Prisciano (Sussidi eruditi 29), Rom 1978, S. 237\endash 238 (Nr. 522). \endash  Zur Textl\u252 \'fccke am Anfang des dritten Kapitels von \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  De metris\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , das auch eine Auflistung der 28 metrischen Pedes beinhaltete, s. zuletzt \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Romanini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , a. O., S. LXXIX\endash LXXX.
\par \pard\sl360\slmult1\fi0\li0\tx420\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \tab (ff. 226v, 25. Z.\endash 227r, 17. Z.) cap. III (Ms. ohne Titel). \endash  (f. 227r, 18. Z.\endash 227v, 17. Z.) cap. IV (Ms. ohne Titel). \endash  (ff. 227v, 18. Z.\endash 228v) cap. V (Ms. ohne Titel; Anfangsworte in Majuskel als \u220 \'dcberschrift); des. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Romanini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , S. 29, 11 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  contentos oportebit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  (f. 229r\endash v) cap. VI (Ms. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Iambica\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ). \endash  (ff. 229v\endash 230r) cap. VII (Ms. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Trochaica\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ). \endash  (f. 230r\endash v) cap. VIII (Ms. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Anapestica\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ). \endash  (ff. 230v\endash 231r) cap. IX (Ms. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Coriambica\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ). \endash  (f. 231r) cap. X (Ms. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Antipasticum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   [!]); des. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Romanini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , S. 47, 6 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  arma ruitque laetus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  (f. 231v) cap. XI (Ms. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Ionicum a maiore\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ). \endash  (ff. 231v\endash 232v) cap. XII (Ms. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Ionicum a minore\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ).}

