\pard\sl360\slmult1\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  8. (ff. 167r\endash 169r) {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Papias}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , \u8249 \'8bElementarium doctrinae rudimentum\u8250 \'9b (Ms. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Ex Papia alias\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  m\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  agist\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 )\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  re\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   [?]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24   verborum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ), ed. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Papias\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Vocabularius, Venedig: Philippus Pincius, 19.IV.1496; BSB-Ink-P-13; GW M29306; ISTC ip00079000. Mit einigen Textabweichungen; in diesen F\u228 \'e4llen vgl. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[1].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17 Isidorus Hispalensis}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Origines I. XXI und XXIII\endash XXV, ed. W. M. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Lindsay\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Isidorus Hispalensis, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf18 Etymologiae sive originum libri XX\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , I, Oxford 1911. \endash  Exzerpte aus dem Buchstaben N, Vocabularius, ff. 108r\endash 114v: (ff. 167r\endash 168r) Nr. 1 (Ms. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  De notis sententiarum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ): f. 112ar, 13. Z. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Nota est figura propria in littere modum posita\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  ... f. 112br, 27. Z. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  cuius similem superiacentem notam invenerit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Vgl. auch Origines I. XXI 1\endash 28. \endash  (f. 168r\endash v) Nr. 2 (Ms. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  De notis distinctionum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ): f. 112br, 27. Z. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  In sententijs pronunciandis \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ... f. 112br, 40. Z. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  et vocatur distinctio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \endash  (f. 168v): Nr. 3 (Ms. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  De notis iuridicis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ): Origines I. XXIII\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24  1 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Quedam littere in libris iuris verborum suorum note sunt, quo scriptio celeris \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Ms. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  celebris\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 )\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24   breviorque fiat \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ... vgl. I. XXIII\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24  2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  quia multos per haec ignorantes decipiebant\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Nr. 4 (Ms. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  De notis militaribus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ): Origines I. XXIV\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24  1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  In breviculis quoque, quibus militum nomina continebantur \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Et potis est nigrum vicio praefingere theta\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \endash  (ff. 168v\endash 169r) Nr. 5 (Ms. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  De notis litterarum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ): Origines I. XXV\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24  2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Cesar Augustus ad filium inter nos notas si vis tales sunt  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Quidam etiam versibus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   (!)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24   scribunt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . \endash  (ff. 169v\endash 170r) leer.}

